{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg6toxu7FBzRqnvLtVMxs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a practical regex:\n\n```regex\n\\bhttps?:\\/\\/(?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]+\\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}(?::\\d{1,5})?(?:\\/[^\\s?#]*)?(?:\\?[^\\s#]*)?(?:#\\S*)?\n```\n\n**Breakdown**\n- `https?://` matches the scheme, `http` or `https`.\n- `(?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]+\\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}` matches the domain, such as `example.com` or `sub.example.co.uk`.\n- `(?::\\d{1,5})?` matches an optional port.\n- `(?:\\/[^\\s?#]*)?` matches an optional path.\n- `(?:\\?[^\\s#]*)?` matches an optional query string.\n- `(?:#\\S*)?` matches an optional fragment.\n\n**Simpler version**, which is often good enough:\n\n```regex\nhttps?:\\/\\/[^\\s/$.?#].[^\\s]*\n```\n\n**Example in Python**\n\n```python\nimport re\n\npattern = re.compile(r'\\bhttps?://(?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]+\\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}(?::\\d{1,5})?(?:/[^\\s?#]*)?(?:\\?[^\\s#]*)?(?:#\\S*)?')\ntext = \"Visit https://example.com/path?q=1#top or http://foo.org.\"\nprint(pattern.findall(text))\n# ['https://example.com/path?q=1#top', 'http://foo.org.']\n```\n\n**Caveats**\n- Trailing punctuation, like the final `.` in the example, can get captured in the path. Strip it afterward with `.rstrip('.,;:!?)')`.\n- It doesn't match `localhost`, IP addresses, or `user:pass@` credentials. To allow `localhost` and IPv4, change the host part to `(?:localhost|\\d{1,3}(?:\\.\\d{1,3}){3}|(?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]+\\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,})`.\n- For strict validation, use a real URL parser (`urllib.parse`, `new URL()`) instead of a regex."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6952,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6952},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_managemen